# The build context is a WHITELIST: everything is excluded, then exactly the
# paths the Dockerfile COPYs are let back in. A file that is not on this list
# cannot reach `docker build` at all, whatever is lying around in enclave/ on
# the build box (test/, node_modules/, tls/, logs, editor backups).
#
# This does not change the image for a clean tree: none of the excluded paths
# is named by a COPY line, and the Dockerfile never COPYs `.`, so this file is
# not itself part of the image. PCR0 is unchanged.
#
# What it cannot do is tell a stray file INSIDE src/ or attest/ from a real
# one. That is scripts/check-build-context.sh's job (run by CI after the sync
# and by build-enclave.sh before the build). Keep the three in step; the test
# enclave/test/buildContext.test.mjs asserts that every COPY source below is
# re-included here and covered there.
*
!attest
!kmstool
!src
!boot.sh
!package.json
!package-lock.json
